From: OdroidLinux SDK
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: no partial power down or clock gating on Amlogic G12A

The G12A parameters set neither power_down nor no_clock_gating, unlike
the older Amlogic parameters (power_down = NONE), so the G12A controller
gets the hardware default, partial power down. When the USB cable is
pulled out the gadget sees a bus suspend and enters partial power down
(PCGCTL 0x1d: STOPPCLK, PWRCLMP, RSTPDWNMODULE). A system suspend in
that state goes on to back up the registers of the powered down core in
dwc2_gadget_backup_critical_registers() (the global ones read back as
zero) and the SoC hangs for good on the endpoint registers. On the
ODROID-GO Ultra (S922X), suspend to idle or to RAM with the USB-C cable
unplugged hung in dwc2_suspend() every time; with the cable plugged in
it worked.

Use no power down, as the other Amlogic SoCs do, and disable clock
gating, the fallback for that case, which stops the clocks the same way
(as for Rockchip, commit ca2dc35e555e "usb: dwc2: Disable clock gating
feature on Rockchip SoCs").

---
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
@@ -190,6 +190,8 @@
 	p->lpm_clock_gating = false;
 	p->besl = false;
 	p->hird_threshold_en = false;
+	p->power_down = DWC2_POWER_DOWN_PARAM_NONE;
+	p->no_clock_gating = true;
 }
 
 static void dwc2_set_amlogic_a1_params(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg)
